{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 149,
    "dDurationMs": 1801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hi I’m Stanley Kubrick."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1950,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just checking to see if you’re paying attention."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3790,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I’m Sareesh Sudhakaran and this is my personal\ntop ten greatest examples of cinematography"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9330,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in cinema."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10330,
    "dDurationMs": 3929,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have a nagging feeling I’ve left out an\nimportant film, but it’s not the one you’re"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14259,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thinking of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15259,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure I’ve not seen every movie, but neither\nhas anybody else who’s ever been alive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19509,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is my list, what I’ve been inspired\nby, and is at best a starting place for you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24609,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to explore this great art."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26449,
    "dDurationMs": 3181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are only two criteria for films to be\non this list."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29630,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From beginning to end, they must be a powerhouse\nof cinematography."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33040,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It can’t be just one shot or scene, but\nthe whole must inspire awe at every passing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38230,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "moment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39230,
    "dDurationMs": 3050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, you can’t have too much visual effects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42280,
    "dDurationMs": 5910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why movies like 2001: A Space Odyssey,\nMetropolis or The Matrix can’t be on this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48190,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "list, but would still be high up on any list."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51630,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Counting down from number ten, because most\ncinematographers can’t count more than f/11"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55770,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anyway, and too many are enamored with f/1\nfor their own good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60090,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "M. Cinematography: Fritz Arno Wagner."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63020,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where do I begin?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64830,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The world of M is so painstakingly created\nand lit you could pass it off as a modern"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70220,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "film."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71220,
    "dDurationMs": 3470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the signs of great cinematography is\nit shouldn’t be outdated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74690,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you think The Third Man is the height of\nfilm noir you missed the train by about 17"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79390,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80390,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There have been films before M that have extreme\nlight and shadow, what they call the expressionsitic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85650,
    "dDurationMs": 1670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "phase of cinema."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87320,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But none are as gorgeous, or as put together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89180,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You don’t feel any of it isn’t real."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90180,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You could almost smell the streets, the feeling\nof being there is so powerful it adds to the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94530,
    "dDurationMs": 5379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "detective story that inspired Hitchcock, and\nyou can work all the way down to Fincher’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99909,
    "dDurationMs": 1401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Seven if you want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101310,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But M stands for ultimate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104290,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number 9."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105290,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sunrise: A Song of Two Humans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108330,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cinematography by Charles Rosher and Karl\nStruss."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111320,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the film most viewers will have not\nheard of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114110,
    "dDurationMs": 2470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Watch these visuals, shot in 1927."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116580,
    "dDurationMs": 2399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You’ll never forget it again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118979,
    "dDurationMs": 3791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even in its simplest scenes, the attention\nto detail is breathtaking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122770,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That huge and crappy camera was positioned\nexactly where it is on purpose."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127290,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The lighting equipment was intolerable by\ntoday’s standards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129310,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The story of its making is legendary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133200,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only film that can come close to this\nin terms of world-building is Metropolis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137790,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also released in 1927."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138790,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it relied a lot on matte paintings, this\none has real sets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141650,
    "dDurationMs": 3709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Large sets made for essentially a love story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145359,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number 8."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146359,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "El Topo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147359,
    "dDurationMs": 1781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cinematographer: Rafael Corkidi."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149140,
    "dDurationMs": 3139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This must have been a tough film to shoot,\nfor so many reasons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152279,
    "dDurationMs": 4731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s controversial, but is Jodorowsky’s\nmasterpiece for the ages."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157010,
    "dDurationMs": 3339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "El Topo was shot mostly in exteriors, with\nnot a lot of lighting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160349,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it made for that with composition and\ncamera technique that shows profound mastery"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164799,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the medium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165799,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I’ve analyzed El Topo in another video so\nI won’t go into much detail here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169999,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number 7."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170999,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rashomon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171999,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cinematographer: Kazuo Miyagawa"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173409,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s the first film in which the camera\nwas pointed at the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176659,
    "dDurationMs": 1901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to me that’s not important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178560,
    "dDurationMs": 5450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Miyagawa used large mirrors to bounce sunlight\nthrough the trees to get exposure and the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184010,
    "dDurationMs": 3699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "claustrophobic feeling of dense foliage all\naround."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187709,
    "dDurationMs": 3441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The forest is a maze you can’t get out of\ncompletely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191150,
    "dDurationMs": 3839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even the woodcutter gets drawn into this vortex,\neven though he’s a regular."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194989,
    "dDurationMs": 4211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let’s also not forget the black rain that\nmade it appear on camera."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199200,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kurosawa emptied oceans of water for this\nscene, but the rain stays on screen to this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203860,
    "dDurationMs": 1109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204969,
    "dDurationMs": 1090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number 6."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206059,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stalker."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207099,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cinematography by these three gentlemen whose\nnames I can’t pronounce."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209219,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Aleksandr Knyazhinskiy, Georgi Rerberg and\nLeonid Kalashnikov]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210219,
    "dDurationMs": 3211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "El Topo was shot in the desert and Rashomon\nwas shot in the forest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213430,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stalker was shot in an abandoned plant that\nmight have killed its director."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217310,
    "dDurationMs": 3149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You could literally use the term, every frame\na painting, to Stalker."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220459,
    "dDurationMs": 4521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s just filled with gorgeous visuals,\neven when it’s showing rot and decay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224980,
    "dDurationMs": 3869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stalker shows what you can achieve with interesting\nlocations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228849,
    "dDurationMs": 4681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To others it’s dead, but to a genius it’s\na universe of new ideas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233530,
    "dDurationMs": 3879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stalker also used two toned coloring to separate\nthe real world from the Zone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237409,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Interestingly, the Zone looks prettier and\nmore serene than the real world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241909,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number 5."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242909,
    "dDurationMs": 1010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Night of the Hunter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243919,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cinematographer: Stanley Cortez."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245999,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Night of the Hunter has such breathtaking\nvisuals you wonder how they did it, even today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250589,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To me it is the epitome of the expressionistic\nlighting style, also called film noir."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255749,
    "dDurationMs": 2441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The film is one great shadow play."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258190,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everytime you think you’ve seen a shot that’s\ngreat, out comes another even more daring"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262120,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263120,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it goes on all the way to the end credits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265490,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Night of the Hunter has the finest use\nof silhouettes I’ve seen, which is not for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269240,
    "dDurationMs": 2239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the mere sake of adding visual variety."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271479,
    "dDurationMs": 5601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They actually form a visual signature, giving\nthe film a frightening rhythm that keeps you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277080,
    "dDurationMs": 1270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on your toes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278350,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Will evil triumph?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279800,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nope."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280800,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cinematography did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281800,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Spoiler alert."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282880,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number 4."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283880,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Barry Lyndon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284880,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cinematographer: John Alcott."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286790,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For most people it’s all about the candles\nand the Zeiss f/0.95 lens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291060,
    "dDurationMs": 4329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To me, the most arresting elements were actually\nthe beauty of the day scenes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295389,
    "dDurationMs": 1551,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How did they expose correctly?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296940,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why are the colors so beautiful?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298150,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don’t know."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299320,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It just looks like one of the great paintings\ncame to life to tell its own story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303300,
    "dDurationMs": 4339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The challenges of lighting interior sets to\nmake it look natural was by itself tough to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307639,
    "dDurationMs": 2731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do with the technology they had back then."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310370,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The world of Barry Lyndon is so rich with\ndetail and texture."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314150,
    "dDurationMs": 5980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every change in weather is felt, every interior\nspace tells a story with light, and of course,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320130,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you need to give out an Oscar just for executing\nStanley Kubrick’s nerve wracking zoom shots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325080,
    "dDurationMs": 3739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What Barry Lyndon taught me is you don’t\nneed fancy tricks and color grading."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328819,
    "dDurationMs": 4821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you know how to light and nail the basics,\nthe result will naturally be stunning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333640,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number 3."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334640,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Blade Runner."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335640,
    "dDurationMs": 1540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cinematographer: Jordan Cronenweth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337180,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might have noticed a trend with this list."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339300,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of them have amazing production design."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341220,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s no wonder that successful cinematographers\nrely a lot on the production designer or art"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345960,
    "dDurationMs": 2799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "director to accomplish their cinematic vision."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348759,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The set and designs of Blade Runner are so\nreal because they’re close to real life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352759,
    "dDurationMs": 4111,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They really sweated the details, and you feel\nyou’re walking in that world along with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356870,
    "dDurationMs": 1060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Deckard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357930,
    "dDurationMs": 4389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you’re looking for a reason why film\nstill holds relevance today, then Blade Runner"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362319,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is your best bet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363939,
    "dDurationMs": 5241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The way film negative reacts to multi-colored\nlighting, the skin tones, the grains and highlight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369180,
    "dDurationMs": 5450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "textures are all so unique to film you’ll\nnever get this look with digital."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374630,
    "dDurationMs": 3339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With most movies you might not be able to\ntell the difference, but with Blade Runner"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377969,
    "dDurationMs": 1331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379300,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They pushed the lighting and cinematography\nto such extremes it shows film in its best"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384080,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385080,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’re still just at number three."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386990,
    "dDurationMs": 2829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What can beat Blade Runner and Barry Lyndon?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389819,
    "dDurationMs": 2051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only two movies, according to me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391870,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number 2."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392870,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Seven Samurai."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393870,
    "dDurationMs": 1819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cinematographer: Asakazu Nakai."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395689,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I can’t believe they did this in 1954."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398409,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I can’t believe they did this, period."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401009,
    "dDurationMs": 6071,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The phrase ‘every frame a painting’ comes\nfrom Seven Samurai and belongs to Seven Samurai."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407080,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Night of the Hunter is close, but was shot\non studio."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409860,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Seven Samurai was shot on location, sometimes\nin the rain, sometimes with wind machines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414680,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With multiple cameras, and lots of action\nand unpredictable horses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418900,
    "dDurationMs": 2290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it looks like perfection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421190,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The camera work, the movement, the compositions,\nthe lighting, you don’t know where one aspect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425550,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of cinematography starts and the other ends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428270,
    "dDurationMs": 4830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If someone asks me what the perfect movie\nlooks like, I ask them to watch Seven Samurai."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433100,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What can beat a perfect movie?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435360,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only the father of the perfect movie can beat\nthe perfect movie."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439410,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number 1."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440410,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Citizen Kane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441410,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cinematographer: Gregg Toland."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442910,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gregg Toland really took cinematography to\nheights people never knew it could go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447280,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He practically taught the world this through\nCitizen Kane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450120,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By sheer count, the number of cinematography\ntechniques perfected in Citizen Kane is only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455280,
    "dDurationMs": 4359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rivalled by the number of techniques displayed\nin The Birth of a Nation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459639,
    "dDurationMs": 2851,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not every frame is a painting in Citizen Kane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462490,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But every frame was almost impossible to pull\noff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465900,
    "dDurationMs": 1889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It looks effortless, but it’s not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467789,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whisper deep focus to most cinematographers\nears and they will wet their pants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472449,
    "dDurationMs": 3921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then tell them they have to do that with long\ncomplicated takes and they’ll give you a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476370,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "million reasons why this can’t be done."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478810,
    "dDurationMs": 5289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it was done, with far modest equipment,\nthrough sheer will and craftsmanship."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484099,
    "dDurationMs": 5201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not only is Citizen Kane the epitome of great\ncinematography, but it’s the finest example"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489300,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a filmmaking masterclass if there ever\nwas one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492240,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you don’t like this video please hit\nlike, because there are plenty of people who"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495660,
    "dDurationMs": 1279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "disagree with you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496939,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you’re upset your favorite film isn’t\non this list please subscribe, because I’ve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500509,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "got more agony coming your way next week."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503449,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And don’t forget to hit the bell you’ll\nsee on the right, why would you want to miss"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505479,
    "dDurationMs": 50,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being schooled?"
    } ]
  } ]
}
